# ChatXiv Token Configuration
#
# HOW TOKEN LOADING WORKS:
#
# 1. DeepXiv SDK reads tokens from environment variable: os.environ["DEEPXIV_TOKEN"]
# 2. Our scripts (scripts/lib/config.py) read THIS .env file and inject the token
#    into os.environ before calling the SDK
# 3. If no token is set anywhere, the SDK auto-registers an anonymous token on
#    first use and saves it to ~/.env (your home directory)
#
# SETUP STEPS:
#
# Option A - Use a registered token:
#   1. Register at https://data.rag.ac.cn/register to get a token (10,000 requests/day)
#   2. Copy this file: cp .env.example .env
#   3. Fill in your token below: DEEPXIV_TOKEN=dxv_1234567890abcdef
#
# Option B - Use auto-registered anonymous token:
#   1. Leave this file as-is (or create an empty .env)
#   2. Run any chatxiv command (e.g., python scripts/chatxiv.py search "test")
#   3. SDK will auto-register and save token to ~/.env (1,000 requests/day)
#   4. (Optional) Copy that token from ~/.env to this project's .env for version control
#
# WHY TWO .env FILES?
# - ~/.env = global, shared by all DeepXiv SDK usage on your machine
# - ./.env = project-local, lets you version control the token with this repo (gitignored)
# Our scripts check both: project .env first, then fall back to ~/.env

DEEPXIV_TOKEN=

# Optional: override the default project root used by the CLI.
# CHATXIV_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/this/repo

# Report language: en (English), zh (Chinese), es (Spanish), fr (French), de (German), ja (Japanese)
# Default: en
REPORT_LANGUAGE=en

# Number of papers to search when conducting research
# Default: 100
SEARCH_LIMIT=100
